---
functor: 1
title: Headings, lists, tables, code
---

set heading(numbering: none)

These parts work as in Markdown, with labels added.

# Headings

```fn
# Fields {#sec:fields}

## Work

### A small point
```

One to six `#` signs give the level. Headings have numbers, for example 2.1. A label in curly brackets at the end lets text refer to the heading: `@sec:fields` shows "Section 1". The rule `set heading(numbering: none)` removes the numbers.

# Lists

```fn
- A point
- Another point

1. First step
2. Second step
```

A list item starts with `- `, `* ` or a number and `. `. Lists do not nest yet.

# Tables

```fn
| Recipe | Result |
|:--|:-:|
| `theta.hat` | $theta.hat$ |
| `in.not` | $in.not$ |
```

The second row sets the alignment of each column: `:--` left, `:-:` centre, `--:` right. A cell can hold math and code.

# Code blocks

A code block starts with three backticks and a language name, and ends with three backticks. Functor shows the code as it is.

# Images

`![alt text](plot.svg)` shows an image. Put an image in a figure block to give it a number and a caption. See [Blocks](document/blocks.html).
